2093 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186571891 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572093 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186571893 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572093 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572093 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572093 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186571798 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572093 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ecbe05ce-5c99-5a55-b52c-2b92b42e1761" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572104 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186571565 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572104 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186571690 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572104 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186571734 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572104 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186571780 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572104 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186571843 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572104 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572104 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572104 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186571780 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572104 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fb846a7c-a839-56a8-a16b-0c31f3561ba1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572109 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572014 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572109 #edb/ref 1069 "q-119791" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572109 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572109 #edb/ref 1071 "The vector $m$ has magnitude $\\frac{7}{2}.$ Find a unit vector that is parallel to $m.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572109 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0ea2b07d-a05f-5f3d-9418-d56ab52d7fcd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572109 #edb/ref 1074 "To obtain the unit vector that is parallel to $m$, we divide $m$ by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{m}{|\\,m\\,|}=\\frac{1}{(\\frac{7}{2})}m=\\frac{2}{7}m\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572119 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572042 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572119 #edb/ref 1069 "q-77227" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572119 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572119 #edb/ref 1071 "The vector $a$ is directed due north-west and $|\\,a\\,|=5$, while the vector $b$ is directed due south-west and $|\\,b\\,|=12.$ Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $a+b?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572119 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2f3e6ef6-a3b7-556b-876b-54d269e801f3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572119 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we have to find $a+b.$ According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant $a+b$ goes from the tail of $a$ to the head of $b:$   \n\n![](images/15/153aff405a3ae0859ff74fcb98deb09e038db7b033cbe54223866c9fe1724fb1.png)\n\nTo find the unit vector corresponding to $a+b,$ we have to divide by the magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the magnitude, first notice that we obtain a right triangle. So, we can use the Pythagorean theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{|a+b|}^{2} & ={|a|}^{2}+{|b|}^{2} \\\\  & ={5}^{2}+{12}^{2} \\\\  & =169\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the magnitude is\n\n$$\n|a+b|=\\sqrt{169}=13,\n$$\n\nand the corresponding unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{13}(a+b).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572126 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572064 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572126 #edb/ref 1069 "q-275632" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572126 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572126 #edb/ref 1071 "The vector $a$ is directed horizontally to the right and has magnitude $\\sqrt{3}$, while the vector $b$ is directed vertically up and has magnitude $\\sqrt{6}.$ Find a unit vector $u$ that is parallel to  $a+b$ and has the same direction as $a+b.$ \n\nType $a$ and $b$ to represent the vectors $a$ and $b,$ respectively.  \n\n$u=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572126 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "46e2433f-faec-5a20-b0d6-cabb5029813a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572126 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we have to find $a+b.$ According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant $a+b$ goes from the tail of $a$ to the head of $b:$ \n\n![](images/b7/b7d45d7cd1ea2c61961da8279d3f8702d3e52092fc6aab75a94d3b5076928dba.png)\n\nTo find the unit vector corresponding to $a+b,$ we have to divide by the magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the magnitude, first notice that we obtain a right triangle. So, we can use the Pythagorean theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{|a+b|}^{2} & ={|a|}^{2}+{|b|}^{2} \\\\  & ={(\\sqrt{3})}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{6})}^{2} \\\\  & =3+6 \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the magnitude is\n\n$$\n|a+b|=\\sqrt{9}=3,\n$$\n\nand the corresponding unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(a+b).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572132 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572070 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572132 #edb/ref 1069 "q-69977" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572132 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572132 #edb/ref 1071 "The vector $\\overset{\\to }{ST}$ has magnitude $6.$ Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $\\overset{\\to }{ST}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572132 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "50b46995-90d3-558d-b802-06393c983f30" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572132 #edb/ref 1074 "To obtain the unit vector that is parallel to $\\overset{\\to }{ST},$ we divide $\\overset{\\to }{ST}$ by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{ST}}{|\\overset{\\to }{ST}|}=\\frac{1}{6}\\overset{\\to }{ST}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572138 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572093 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572138 #edb/ref 1069 "q-77229" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572138 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572138 #edb/ref 1071 "The vector $a$ is directed due north-east and $|\\,a\\,|=7$, while the vector $b$ is directed due north-west and $|\\,b\\,|=7.$ Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $a+b?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572138 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "64f8dbbc-bd8d-5e6e-b9e2-32a2e83cd44b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572138 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we have to find $a+b.$ According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant $a+b$ goes from the tail of $a$ to the head of $b:$   \n\n![](images/94/9468530a650f0bee117a4254aa87b5954c7bbbe2684d95f9db3f9961026abcb2.png)\n\nTo find the unit vector corresponding to $a+b,$ we have to divide by the magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the magnitude, first notice that we obtain a right triangle. So, we can use the Pythagorean theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{|a+b|}^{2} & ={|a|}^{2}+{|b|}^{2} \\\\  & ={7}^{2}+{7}^{2} \\\\  & =98\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the magnitude is\n\n$$\n|a+b|=\\sqrt{98}=7\\sqrt{2},\n$$\n\nand the corresponding unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7\\sqrt{2}}(a+b).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572156 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572104 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572156 #edb/ref 1069 "q-11377" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572156 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572156 #edb/ref 1071 "The vector $b$ has magnitude $20.$ Find a unit vector that is parallel to $b.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572156 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9630409b-82f5-5e41-add3-624263d041a1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572156 #edb/ref 1074 "To obtain the unit vector that is parallel to $b$, we divide $b$ by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{b}{|\\,b\\,|}=\\frac{1}{20}b\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572174 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572053 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572174 #edb/ref 1069 "q-275627" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572174 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572174 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/13/13fc8ff564a7162c556d050a10df6e8f23c0fca269e3b88168ca6681be3ad3a3.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Find a unit vector $u$ that is parallel to  $p+q$ and has the same direction as $p+q.$ \n\nType $p$ and $q$ to represent the vectors $p$ and $q,$ respectively.  \n\n$u=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572174 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bf062e19-facf-5f56-9031-7ed68b8d30bc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572174 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we have to find $p+q.$ According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant $p+q$ goes from the tail of $p$ to the head of $q:$ \n\n![](images/68/68c14ce5ff66272986e958f09f30289d56519e90b34fae23362753f84c042a50.png)\n\nIn $△AHB$, we have $∠AHB={90}^{∘}$, $AH=2$ and $BH=3.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|p+q| & =AB \\\\  & =\\sqrt{A{H}^{2}+B{H}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2)^{2}+(3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $p+q$ is $\\sqrt{13}.$ Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{1}{|p+q|}\\cdot (p+q) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}(p+q).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572179 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572055 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572179 #edb/ref 1069 "q-119796" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572179 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572179 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/aa/aa72f6ea8c52a1f141f8469c3f932937b8b957956dc478811910e77c83336a9c.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $p?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572179 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cb1f02a3-6465-553f-a943-f356abc8fd01" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572179 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/4d/4d4d7faa0c0611c8ef891cda5fef3b75a61aa97e0879fac525f58f4ce263c937.png)\n\nIn $△AHB$, we have $∠AHB={90}^{∘}$, $AH=2$ and $BH=5.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\sqrt{A{H}^{2}+B{H}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{29}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $p$ is $\\sqrt{29}.$ Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{1}{|\\,p\\,|}\\cdot p \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{29}}p.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572196 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572020 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572196 #edb/ref 1069 "q-119788" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572196 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572196 #edb/ref 1071 "The vector $\\overset{\\to }{UV}$ has magnitude $\\frac{1}{3}.$ Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $\\overset{\\to }{UV}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572196 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ec3ac6e6-c786-5106-a626-b9bded90e31e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572196 #edb/ref 1074 "To obtain the unit vector that is parallel to $\\overset{\\to }{UV},$ we divide $\\overset{\\to }{UV}$ by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{UV}}{|\\overset{\\to }{UV}|}=\\frac{1}{(\\frac{1}{3})}\\overset{\\to }{UV}=3\\overset{\\to }{UV}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
